---
import styles from "@context-path/components/context.module.css";
---

<section class={styles.section}>
	<h1>my context</h1>

	<article class={styles.content}>
		<p>
			Since I was a kid, and not so much of a kid, I've always liked doing lots
			of completely different things, although I didn't realize it until
			recently. I went from playing volleyball and football to competing in
			CrossFit, and in my studies, from sports science to chemical engineering
			to the firefighter entrance exams, which I almost passed. But nothing
			fulfilled me. Everything bored me.
		</p>
		<p>
			I'd love to say that since I was a kid I knew what I wanted to do and that
			I was part of that exclusive club of six-year-olds who could already code.
			It would have saved me a lot of time, but I had to take my share of hits
			and wait for a pandemic to get bored enough to stop and think about what I
			wanted to do with my life. That's how I made my first discovery:
			technology. I haven't stopped thinking about it since.
		</p>
		<p>
			For most of my life I've been self-taught, which led me to code in JS/TS
			and to sharpen my judgment about what to do and learn, and what and who to
			listen to. By then I was well on my way, and hooked, to figuring out my
			career when I stumbled upon something even more interesting: the startup
			world.
		</p>
		<p>
			It blew my mind. Now I wanted to know not only how startups are built, but
			also how they understand their users and grow so fast. That discovery led
			me to what I now consider my four areas of expertise: how to build good
			products, what good design is, why users, and people in general, do what
			they do, and how it all comes together so a company can scale at speed.
		</p>
		<p>
			From then on, everything I do day to day as a growth product engineer,
			from how I think to the books I read, the content I consume, and much of
			my free time, is focused on getting better at each of those areas and at
			connecting them. Including what I write about on <a
				target="_blank"
				rel="me noopener"
				href="https://c12z.io"
				>c12z.io</a
			>.
		</p>
		<p>
			One of the perks of all this is that I'll never get bored. There's always
			something to do, improve, or learn :)
		</p>
		<p>P.S. I'm Chema Ferrández ✌🏽</p>
	</article>
</section>
